{"step_index":2208,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:05:32Z","input_tokens":2527,"cache_read_tokens":212661,"output_tokens":1596,"thinking":"Analyzing how to generate a pattern teaching guide from problem data. The guide will focus on demonstrating the pattern's value by contrasting it with brute-force approaches. Emphasis will be placed on highlighting the core computational invariant that makes the pattern efficient.\n\n\nThe teaching guide will cover patterns like binary search and dynamic programming, focusing on how they reduce computational complexity. Prerequisite concepts such as array indexing, recursion base cases, and stack invariants need to be covered. The guide will include illustrative examples to solidify understanding and a clear three-step explanation: Setup, Process, Return. Edge cases will also be addressed. The primary goal will be to clarify the pattern's behavior and the value of pattern-based solution approaches.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"const fs = require('fs');\\nconst vm = require('vm');\\nconst path = require('path');\\n\\nconst engineCode = fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', 'scratch', 'code-flow-visualizer', 'app_build', 'engine.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst sandbox = { console, Math, Number, String, Array, Object, Set, Map, JSON, Date, window: {} };\\nvm.createContext(sandbox);\\nvm.runInContext(engineCode, sandbox);\\n\\nconst PythonExecutionEngine = sandbox.window.PythonExecutionEngine;\\nconst engine = new PythonExecutionEngine();\\n\\n// Prototype function runner\\nfunction runPythonFunction(userCode, funcName, args) {\\n  // Construct wrapper script that defines function and executes call\\n  const argsJson = JSON.stringify(args).slice(1, -1); // strip [ and ]\\n  const harness = `\\n${userCode}\\n\\n__test_result__ = ${funcName}(${argsJson})\\nprint(\\\"__RESULT__:\\\", __test_result__)\\n`;\\n\\n  const trace = engine.t