{"step_index":2230,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:09:25Z","input_tokens":2871,"cache_read_tokens":228015,"output_tokens":2176,"thinking":"Analyzing the sub-navigation HTML to understand how the tab buttons are rendered and their active states. The `currentSubTab` variable appears to control the \"active\" class assignment, which dynamically updates the visual presentation of the selected tab. Checking how this variable is updated to determine the state management logic.\n\n\nThe `renderProblemWorkspace` function is responsible for dynamically generating the problem-solving environment's content. It renders the breadcrumb for navigation and actions, dynamically displaying content based on the `problemId`. The workspace view is activated when the `currentSubTab` is set to \"workspace\" and displays the problem workspace based on the `activeWorkspaceProblemId` or defaults to 1 if it is not set.\n\n\nThe structure appears to be a problem-solving environment with distinct sections for understanding the problem and learning patterns. The \"Understand the Problem\" tab offers a breakdown into problem overview, goals, examples, constraints, and edge cases. The \"Learn the Pattern\" tab provides pattern identification, justification, prerequisites, and a small example. This setup seems designed to guide a user through a structured problem-solving process.\n\n\nThe problem-solving environment is structured with an interactive practice area providing a code editor, testing features, hints, and a visual execution tool. A structured \"recipe\" approach, breaking the solution into setup, process, and return phases, is the intended strategy for solving problems. It seems designed to guide users through the process step-by-step.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# scratch/build_phase5_workspace.py\\n# Implements Phase 5: Problem Learning Workspace in dsa_dashboard.js\\nimport os\\nimport re\