{"step_index":2246,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:12:18Z","input_tokens":3885,"cache_read_tokens":244044,"output_tokens":8531,"thinking":"Analyzing click event handlers within the workspace context. Found handlers for opening workspaces by ID, navigating back to problem listings, and handling workspace tab selections. The workspace tab handler retrieves the tab side attribute to determine the correct tab.\n\n\nThe tab selection handler updates the workspace state, showing or hiding panes based on the selected tab and side (left/right). Active tab buttons are updated dynamically to reflect user selection.\n\nThe code run button handler retrieves code from an editor and saves it. It then executes the code and displays any errors in a console output area, properly escaping HTML to prevent injection vulnerabilities.\n\n\nThe code execution handler displays output, including standard output and final variable values, indicating a successful run. A separate handler is identified for running tests.\n\nThe test execution handler retrieves code, saves it, and then runs tests, updating a badge to show the number of passed/total tests and the percentage. The test results panel is made visible.\n\n\nThe test results are rendered dynamically, indicating pass/fail status through visual cues and detailed input/output comparisons, including error messages. The test summary updates a badge and console output with the total, passed, and failed test counts.\n\nA handler is also present for a reset code button. This handler will revert the code editor to its original starter template after confirmation.\n\n\nExamining the reset code button handler, it retrieves the starter code and saves the current user code. An autosave status message is then displayed, confirming the reset operation.\n\nThe hint button handler increments the revealed hint count up to the maximum available for the active problem, rerendering the workspace.\n\nThe reveal solution button handler toggles the visibility of the reference solution after user confirmation, also rerendering the workspace.\n\nThe copy reference solution button handler retrieves the problem's reference solution and inserts it into the code editor.\n\n\nAnalyzing handlers for copying the reference solution, visualizing it, and visualizing user code, along with a handler to create shareable problem links. The copy solution handler fetches either the reference or starter code and inserts it into the editor. Visualization handlers are present for both reference and user code; they retrieve code from the appropriate source (reference/starter or editor) for visualization.\n\nThe shareable link handler constructs a URL for the active problem, using the window's origin and pathname. It falls back to a hash-based URL if the window object or clipboard is unavailable, though the analysis stops there.\n\n\nThe code snippet handling the shareable link creation attempts to write the constructed URL to the clipboard using an API, falling back to a hash-based URL if the API isn't available. The handler associated with the code editor saves the user's code on every change. The function that loads and visualizes the problem is inspecting to see if an overriding code value exists or defaulting to the starter code and then updating a visualizer component with the code.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# scratch/apply_phase5_events_and_router.py\\nimport os\\n\\nwith open('app_build/dsa_dashboard.js', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    code = f.read()\\n\\n# 1. Update loadAndVisualizeProblem to accept optional codeOverride\\ntarget_load_vis = \\\"\\\"\\\"    loadAndVisualizeProblem(id) {\\n      const problem = this.problemsById.get(id);\\n      if (!problem) return;\\n\\n      this.activeVisualizerProblemId = id;\\n      this.markAttempted(id);\\n\\n      if (window.teachMeApp) {\\n        window.teachMeApp.sourceCode = problem.starterCode;\\n        if (window.teachMeApp.codeTextarea) {\\n          window.teachMeApp.codeTextarea.value = problem.starterCode;\\n        }\\n        window.teachMeApp.inputCode = '';\\n        window.teachMeApp.currentPresetKey = 'custom';\\n        window.teachMeApp.analyzeAndRun();\\n      }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nreplacement_load_vis = \\\"\\\"\\\"    loadAndVisualizeProblem(id, codeOverride = null) {\\n      const problem = this.problemsById.get(id);\\n      if (!problem) return;\\n\\n      this.activeVisualizerProblemId = id;\\n      this.markAttempted(id);\\n\\n      const codeToLoad = codeOverride || this.getUserCode(id) || problem.starterCode;\\n\\n      if (window.teachMeApp) {\\n        window.teachMeApp.sourceCode = codeToLoad;\\n        if (window.teachMeApp.codeTextarea) {\\n          window.teachMeApp.codeTextarea.value = codeToLoad;\\n        }\\n        window.teachMeApp.inputCode = '';\\n        window.teachMeApp.currentPresetKey = 'custom';\\n        window.teachMeApp.analyzeAndRun();\\n      }\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nassert target_load_vis in code, \\\"target_load_vis not found\\\"\\ncode = code.replace(target_load_vis, replacement_load_vis, 1)\\n\\n# 2. Update visualizer banner with button to return to Workspace\\ntarget_banner_actions = \\\"\\\"\\\"          <div class=\\\"dsa-active-actions\\\">\\n            ${isSolved \\n              ? `<span class=\\\"solved-pill\\\">✅ Solved</span>` \\n              : `<button id=\\\"btnBannerMarkSolved\\\" class=\\\"btn-banner-solve\\\" title=\\\"Mark this problem as completed\\\">✓ Mark as Solved</button>`}\\n            <button \n<truncated 19425 bytes>","Description":"\"Apply Part 4 of Phase 5 Workspace\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef\\\\scratch\\\\apply_phase5_events_and_router.py\"","toolAction":"\"Creating apply_phase5_events_and_router.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Apply workspace events and router\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
